e order, useful for categorizing its importance to biodegradability.\ndf['ranked_HyWi'] = df['HyWi_B(m)'].rank()", "# is_high_Cp\n# Binary flag indicating if nCp (number of terminal primary C atoms) is greater than 2.\n# Usefulness: Categorizes molecules into high and low terminal C atoms, which affects structural properties.\ndf['is_high_Cp'] = (df['nCp'] > 2).astype(int)", "# bin_C_percent\n# Binned categories for percentage of Carbon atoms (C%).\n# Usefulness: Groups C% into broader categories to capture general trends in Carbon influence.\ndf['bin_C_percent'] = pd.cut(df['C%'], bins=[0, 20, 40, 60, 80], labels=[1, 2, 3, 4])", "# rolling_mean_SM6_L\n# 3-sample rolling mean of SM6_L.\n# Usefulness: Captures the short-term trend in spectral moment order 6, highlighting local behavior.\ndf['rolling_mean_SM6_L'] = df['SM6_L'].rolling(window=3).mean()", "# reciprocal_Ti2_L\n# Reciprocal transformation on TI2_L.\n# Usefulness: Addresses potential non-linear relationships by exploring the inverse scaling effect of TI2_L on biodegradability.\ndf['reciprocal_Ti2_L'] = 1 / (df['TI2_L'] + 1e-6)", "# abs_Psi_i_1d\n# Absolute value of Psi_i_1d.\n# Usefulness: Eliminates the directional effect to explore magnitude-only impacts of pseudoconnectivity.\ndf['abs_Psi_i_1d'] = df['Psi_i_1d'].abs()", "df.drop(columns=['nCrt'], inplace=True)", "df.drop(columns=['B04[C-Br]'], inplace=True)", "df.drop(columns=['N-073'], inplace=True)"]
